    "compiler_level_findings": [
      "SYMBOL RULE CORRECTED: the high half of a lui/lw/sw/addiu materialisation is ALWAYS truncating; the declared value V must satisfy V>>16 == hi and V&0xffff == lo16. The earlier \"addiu rounds its hi half\" rule was an artifact of declaring the Ghidra address and letting the compiler use it faithfully.",
